<body>
<main class="presentation">
<section class="slide" id="title-slide">
  <div class="kicker">Stack Overflow Developer Survey 2024</div>
  <div class="content title-grid">
    <div>
      <h1>Developer Workforce & Compensation Trends</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Key findings for engineering managers and HR leaders benchmarking developer compensation, hiring strategy, and workplace expectations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="scale-card">
      <div class="big-number">65,437<small>survey respondents</small></div>
      <div class="big-number" style="font-size:clamp(2.4rem,5.4vw,5.5rem)">180+<small>countries represented</small></div>
      <p style="margin:0;color:#d3ded9">Source: Stack Overflow 2024 Developer Survey, Work section.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <footer><span>Developer workforce + pay benchmarks</span><span>01 / 08</span></footer>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="employment-status-overview">
  <header><div><div class="kicker">Employment status</div><h2>84% of Developers Are Working, but Full-Time Employment Dips in the U.S.</h2></div><div class="header-rule"></div></header>
  <div class="content two-col">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Global respondent mix</h3>
      <div class="metric-row">
        <div class="metric"><b>84%</b><span>currently working</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><b>69%</b><span>full-time</span></div>
        <div class="metric"><b>16.4%</b><span>freelance / contract</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="stacked" aria-label="Global employment status stacked bar">
        <div class="seg" style="width:69%;background:var(--green)">69%</div>
        <div class="seg" style="width:16.4%;background:var(--orange)">16.4%</div>
        <div class="seg" style="width:13.2%;background:var(--blue)">13.2%</div>
        <div class="seg" style="width:1.4%;background:#9aa6a2"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="legend"><span><i style="background:var(--green)"></i>Full-time</span><span><i style="background:var(--orange)"></i>Freelance</span><span><i style="background:var(--blue)"></i>Student</span></div>
      <p>Full-time employment remains the dominant mode, followed by independent contracting/freelancing and full-time students.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <div class="big-number" style="font-size:clamp(2.7rem,6vw,6.2rem)">64.8%<small>U.S. full-time in 2024</small></div>
      <p>U.S. full-time employment dropped from 69% in 2023 to 64.8% in 2024 — a roughly four-point decline.</p>
      <p>Non-full-time patterns vary by market: the U.K. and Ukraine lean toward contracting, while Germany and India skew toward students.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <footer><span>Source: Stack Overflow 2024 Survey, Employment Status</span><span>02 / 08</span></footer>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="work-environment-shift">
  <header><div><div class="kicker">Work environment</div><h2>In-Person Work Rises to 20% While Hybrid Holds Steady at 42%</h2></div><div class="header-rule"></div></header>
  <div class="content two-col">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Three-year arrangement trend</h3>
      <div class="trend" aria-label="Remote hybrid in-person work trend">
        <div class="year"><div class="columns"><div class="col" style="height:38%;background:var(--teal)">38</div><div class="col" style="height:42%;background:var(--green)">42</div><div class="col" style="height:15%;background:var(--orange)">15</div></div><div class="year-label">2022</div></div>
        <div class="year"><div class="columns"><div class="col" style="height:38%;background:var(--teal)">38</div><div class="col" style="height:42%;background:var(--green)">42</div><div class="col" style="height:16%;background:var(--orange)">16</div></div><div class="year-label">2023</div></div>
        <div class="year"><div class="columns"><div class="col" style="height:38%;background:var(--teal)">38</div><div class="col" style="height:42%;background:var(--green)">42</div><div class="col" style="height:20%;background:var(--orange)">20</div></div><div class="year-label">2024</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="legend"><span><i style="background:var(--teal)"></i>Remote</span><span><i style="background:var(--green)"></i>Hybrid</span><span><i style="background:var(--orange)"></i>In-person</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Benchmarking implication</h3>
      <ul class="note-list">
        <li><strong>Hybrid is still the center of gravity:</strong> 42% in 2024, consistent with 2023.</li>
        <li><strong>Remote remains material:</strong> 38% of respondents report remote work.</li>
        <li><strong>Return-to-office is gradual:</strong> in-person increased from 15% to 16% to 20% over three years.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <footer><span>Source: Stack Overflow 2024 Survey, Work Environment Trends</span><span>03 / 08</span></footer>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="salary-by-developer-type">
  <header><div><div class="kicker">Salary by developer type</div><h2>Senior Executives and Dev Advocates Top $124K+ Median Salary</h2></div><div class="header-rule"></div></header>
  <div class="content two-col" style="grid-template-columns:1.35fr .65fr">
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Top 10 roles by median compensation (USD)</h3>
      <div class="bar-chart" aria-label="Horizontal bar chart of median salary by developer type">
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Senior Executive</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:100%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$127K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Dev Advocate</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:97.5%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$124K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Manager</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:91.1%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$116K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Dev Experience</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:86.0%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$109K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">SRE</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:77.8%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$99K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Cloud Infra.</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:75.9%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$97K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Blockchain</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:67.5%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$86K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Product Manager</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:62.8%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$80K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Full-stack</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:49.7%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$63K</div></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><div class="bar-label">Front-end</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:38.3%"></div></div><div class="bar-value">$49K</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <div class="pill">22,677 salary responses</div>
      <p>Leadership and developer relations roles command the premium end of the market.</p>
      <p>Among purely technical roles, SRE and cloud infrastructure engineers are highest-paid in the provided benchmark set.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <footer><span>Data: source brief; figure reference: figure_1.jpg</span><span>04 / 08</span></footer>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="salary-vs-experience-scatter">
  <header><div><div class="kicker">Experience vs. salary</div><h2>Experience Pays: Top Roles Combine 14+ Years with Six-Figure Salaries</h2></div><div class="header-rule"></div></header>
  <div class="content scatter-wrap">
    <div class="scatter" aria-label="Scatter plot of median salary vs average years experience by developer type">
      <div class="axis-y">Median salary (USD)</div><div class="axis-x">Average years experience</div>
      <span class="dot lg" style="--x:.94;--y:1;--c:var(--green)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.94;--y:1">Senior Exec</span>
      <span class="dot lg" style="--x:.88;--y:.973;--c:var(--green)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.88;--y:.973">Dev Advocate</span>
      <span class="dot lg" style="--x:.82;--y:.915;--c:var(--green)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.82;--y:.915">Manager</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.65;--y:.855;--c:var(--teal)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.65;--y:.855">Dev Experience</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.53;--y:.762;--c:var(--teal)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.53;--y:.762">Cloud Infra.</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.35;--y:.784;--c:var(--teal)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.35;--y:.784">SRE</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.29;--y:.662;--c:var(--orange)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.29;--y:.662">Blockchain</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.76;--y:.608;--c:var(--orange)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.76;--y:.608">Product Mgr</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.35;--y:.459;--c:var(--blue)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.35;--y:.459">Full-stack</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.24;--y:.326;--c:var(--blue)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.24;--y:.326">Front-end</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.00;--y:.00;--c:var(--red)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.00;--y:.00">Student</span>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Pattern to benchmark</h3>
      <ul class="note-list">
        <li>Senior Executive, Dev Advocate, and Manager roles pair 15+ years with top median compensation.</li>
        <li>Dev Experience sits above $109K with roughly 12 years of experience.</li>
        <li>Student is the visible low-salary outlier at $15K and roughly 2 years.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <footer><span>Data: source brief; figure reference: figure_2.jpg</span><span>05 / 08</span></footer>
</section>

<section class="slide" id="salary-by-language">
  <header><div><div class="kicker">Salary by language</div><h2>Erlang & Clojure Developers Earn &gt;$95K; Dart & Prolog Below $45K</h2></div><div class="header-rule"></div></header>
  <div class="content scatter-wrap">
    <div class="scatter" aria-label="Scatter plot of median salary vs average experience by programming language">
      <div class="axis-y">Median salary (USD)</div><div class="axis-x">Average years experience</div>
      <span class="dot lg" style="--x:.59;--y:1;--c:var(--green)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.59;--y:1">Erlang</span>
      <span class="dot lg" style="--x:.53;--y:.963;--c:var(--green)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.53;--y:.963">Clojure</span>
      <span class="dot lg" style="--x:.53;--y:.926;--c:var(--green)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.53;--y:.926">Elixir</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:1;--y:.870;--c:var(--teal)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:1;--y:.870">Perl</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.53;--y:.852;--c:var(--teal)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.53;--y:.852">Ruby</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.41;--y:.833;--c:var(--teal)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.41;--y:.833">Scala</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.41;--y:.611;--c:var(--orange)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.41;--y:.611">Go</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.41;--y:.444;--c:var(--blue)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.41;--y:.444">Python</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.47;--y:.389;--c:var(--blue)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.47;--y:.389">JavaScript</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.47;--y:.111;--c:var(--red)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.47;--y:.111">PHP</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.35;--y:.019;--c:var(--red)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.35;--y:.019">Dart</span>
      <span class="dot" style="--x:.41;--y:0;--c:var(--red)"></span><span class="dot-label" style="--x:.41;--y:0">Prolog</span>
    </div>
    <div class="panel">
      <h3>Language premium signal</h3>
      <ul class="note-list">
        <li>Niche functional languages lead: Erlang (~$97K), Clojure (~$95K), Elixir (~$93K).</li>
        <li>Mainstream JavaScript (~$64K) and PHP (~$49K) sit below the top cluster.</li>
        <li>The overall reported salary range dropped roughly $10K versus 2023.</li>
      </ul>
